calls:
k: On the record
Petra Solano of Crestfall, twenty-two. Nominated by a Vowed officer and approved by the Crown (TR). She matters by doing less (WR 28).
||
k: Her fate
note: Her death.
Dies before Phase Two. The Empire calls it a sudden medical event, and it isn't (TR). Her death costs the Trial nothing, and her status goes back to her family (FR 23–24).
/end

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · X · PETRA · THE RECORD AND HER DOMINION" m="TKC: TR · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:mountain} · {v1:lived5}"
# Crestfall
plate: doc
dh: Covenant Registry | MOUNTAIN DOMINION · CRESTFALL
df: Candidate | SOLANO, Petra · twenty-two
df: Nominated by | a Vowed officer (TR)
df: Approved by | the Crown (TR)
df: Stated purpose | the Trials
df: Actual purpose | ____________
stamp: COVENANT DAUGHTER
/end
rec:
The boy next door | She grew up beside a family whose youngest son she loved, the way children who grow up together do. The family relocated where she couldn't follow, and she kept looking, the way you look for something you believe can still be found (TR).
Why she entered | To get into the Crownward, where the records and archives are. The boy disappeared into Mountain terrain four years ago, and the official record doesn't hold his name (TR).
Why she was chosen | POSSIBLE: Someone in the Crown's advisory structure suspected she was looking for something and wanted her looking where they could intercept it. If so, the control failed (TR).
Her Dominion | Crestfall is the face and the mountains are the truth. Girls chosen at Designation for classified Vowed service disappear from public life (DOM).
prompt: The boy's name, as she knew it | 3

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · X · PETRA · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TR · DOM · WR 28; VOL. I · {v1:mountain} · {v1:lived5}"
# What she believes
rec:
What she believes | INFERENCE: That what's lost can still be found if you keep looking (TR).
Who taught her | Crestfall, where discipline mattered before the Empire made it doctrine. Families take their sons above the city the night before assessment and show them the mountains, which were there before the Empire and will be there after (MEN).
What she practices | The Witness Walk. The name spoken once, directly to the mountain, which Crestfall trusts more than God or the Temple, and then the long walk down where the grief happens (DOM).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a woman like her
POSSIBLE: The Temple reads the Song of Songs only as an allegory of Christ and the church, which is an old and real tradition, so the Song's woman searching the streets for the one she loves is never read as a woman.
/end
prompt: What she says to the mountain, and whose name | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · X · PETRA · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="MATT 16.18; SONG 3.1–4; SONG 5.6–7; SONG 8.6"
# The text
note: Her death.
rec:
Her name | Greek *petra*, "rock," the word behind "upon this rock I will build my church" (Matt 16.18, Vol. I, {v1:cast}).
The woman searching · Song 3 | POSSIBLE: "I will rise now, and go about the city… I will seek him whom my soul loveth" (3.2). She finds him and won't let him go. **Where it breaks:** Petra goes about the city and finds the archive instead.
The watchmen · Song 5.7 | POSSIBLE: The second time she searches, "the watchmen that went about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me." **Where it breaks:** The Song keeps going after the watchmen. Petra's story doesn't.
tab:
| She'd quote | Never read to her |
| Song 3.2, "I will seek him whom my soul loveth" | Song 5.7, the watchmen |
| _ | Song 8.6, "love is strong as death" |
box: Volume One
Mountain, {v1:mountain}. Lived religion, {v1:lived5}. The three arguments, with the Song of Songs, {v1:b-proverbs}. The ledger and the Dissent, {v1:ledger}.
/end

